## Why This Is Asked
This question probes concrete E2E strategies for feature flags in multi-tenant, latency-sensitive systems, ensuring isolation, observability, and fast rollback.

## Key Concepts
- Feature flags, canary rollout, rollback semantics
- Multi-tenant data isolation and tenant-scoped routing
- End-to-end with API mocks, network latency, and analytics verification
- Cross-browser/mobile coverage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright snippet (conceptual)
test('feature-flag canary rollout', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/api/flags/**', route => route.fulfill({ status: 200, body: JSON.stringify({ flag: true }) }));
  // navigate to onboarding
  await page.goto('/onboarding');
  // assert canary UI visible only when flag on
  const el = page.locator('#instant-onboard');
  await expect(el).toBeVisible();
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
